17:03:13 [f463]    - under         (lower than / underneath)
17:03:13 [f463]    - behind        (further from the camera, partially hidden)
17:03:13 [f463]    - in_front_of   (closer to camera, may partially block the other)
17:03:13 [f463]    - in            (inside / contained by the other; partially hidden by its walls or rim)
17:03:13 [f463]    - out           (outside / not contained by the other; fully visible and separate)
17:03:13 [f463]    - other         (none of the above clearly applies)
17:03:13 [f463] 4. Does that match the requested relation 'next_to'?
