rt, child-friendly explanation>\"\n}\nUse the criteria to determine `obj_a_found`, `obj_b_found` and `actual_relation.`\nDo not set `actual_relation` to a preposition that is not in the criteria, i.e. on, next to, etc.\nSet `correct` to true if and only if both objects are found and the actual relation matches the requested relation.\nSet `reason` to a short explanation for the child to understand your verdict.\nIf `correct`=false and `actual_relation`!=other, include `actual_relation` in `reason`.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"obj_a_found\": true,\n  \"obj_b_found\": true,\n  \"actual_relation\": \"other\",\n  \"correct\": false,\n  \"reason\": \"The lemon is next to the apple instead of behind it.\"\n}"}
